$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM [1,1':4',1''-Terphenyl]-2'-yl(phenyl)methanone (3a): A mixture of 2a
(1.70 g, 5 mmol), benzeneboronic acid (1.46 g, 12 mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (0.35
g, 0.3 mmol), and potassium carbonate (2.76 g, 20 mmol) in 200 mL of
toluene/ethanol/water (8/1/1 v/v/v) was heated to reflux for 12 h under
nitrogen. The reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature, poured
into water, and extracted twice with dichloromethane. The combined
organic layers were washed with saturated brine solution and water, and
dried over anhydrous magnesium sulfate. After filtration and solvent
evaporation, the residue was purified by silica-gel column chromatography
using hexane/dichloromethane as eluent. White solid, yield 91% (1.52 g).
1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.82 (dd, J = 8.0, 1.9 Hz, 1H), 7.75 (d, J =
1.7 Hz, 1H), 7.71 (d, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H), 7.68-7.66 (m, 2H), 7.58 (d, J =
8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.49-7.46 (m, 2H), 7.44-7.37 (m, 2H), 7.32-7.28 (m, 4H),
7.24-7.21 (m, 2H), 7.19-7.16 (m, 1H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 198.7,
140.0, 139.9, 139.8, 139.5, 137.4, 132.9, 130.6, 130.0, 129.1, 129.0,
128.9, 128.3, 128.2, 127.8, 127.4, 127.3, 127.1. LC-MS (APCI): m/z 335.2
(C25H18O, calcd 334.1358).
